# check: fail error[G17]: this generic's instantiations never end - each one requires a larger one
# G17: an array taken by value whose body decides something on its length (an array made of it, D9a) is an instance per
# length (G29), and one asking for an instance of a larger length each time never ends - G17's bound stops it (D9c's
# 128-byte cap, which stopped it first, went on 2026-11-01)
fn grow(a Array<I64>) I64 {
    b := Array<I64>(a.Len() + 1)
    return grow(b)
}
fn main() ? {
    a := Array<I64>(1)
    x := grow(a)
}
